<https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/soc2> a owl:Ontology ;
    dct:title "AICPA SOC 2 — Trust Services Criteria (Security / Common Criteria)"@en ;
    dct:description "OWL + SHACL projection of the Interego substrate's SOC 2 mapping (https://markjspivey-xwisee.github.io/interego/ns/soc2): the Common Criteria for logical and physical access (CC6.1–CC6.8), for responding to security incidents (CC7.3–CC7.5) and for change management (CC8.1), and the operational evidence events Interego records, each an operation an auditor can sample as evidence for a criterion: an access change for CC6.2 and CC6.3, a deploy for CC8.1. Composed into PGSL and projected here so a cited control IRI dereferences."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Independent formalization by Mark Spivey (Foxxi Mediums Inc.). Not affiliated with or endorsed by the AICPA. Where this document and the published standard differ, the standard governs."@en ,
        "Mapped to the Interego substrate's SOC 2 vocabulary (prefix soc2:, https://markjspivey-xwisee.github.io/interego/ns/soc2) by SKOS mappings."@en ,
        "Each criterion is paraphrased and cited by its code; the AICPA's text governs. How Interego produces evidence for one is documented with the substrate (https://github.com/markjspivey-xwisee/interego/blob/foxxi-ns-2026.10.0/spec/SOC2-PREPARATION.md), not here: whether the evidence suffices is the auditor's judgment."@en ,
        "The criteria are the concepts of one list (CommonCriterion), each a TrustServicesCriterion: the class and the list name the same criteria, so an event that cites a concept (evidences) cites a criterion."@en ,
        "An instance written as JSON is read into this ontology through the JSON-LD 1.1 context published at https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/soc2/context/2026.10.0, which is generated from this document. The shapes at https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/soc2/shapes/2026.10.0 constrain that reading, and the Foxxi validator (POST https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/soc2/validate) checks the JSON against the same shapes."@en ,
        "The shapes select a node by its class (sh:targetClass) and, as the RDFS domain and range rules make a node an instance of a class, by a property it has (sh:targetSubjectsOf) or by the property that reaches it (sh:targetObjectsOf): a node is checked whether or not it declares its type. The Foxxi validator selects the same nodes of the JSON, and every result cites its shape."@en ,
        "Earlier publications served this document's terms under https://interego-foxxi-bridge.livelysky-8b81abb0.eastus.azurecontainerapps.io/ns/soc2#, on a host since retired. A term IRI in that namespace names the term with the same local name in this one; the Foxxi validator reads it so, and nothing is published there any more."@en ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/soc2/2026.10.0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "2026.10.0" ;
    skos:historyNote "Versioned by calendar (YYYY.MM.PATCH) from 2026.10.0: the version numbers this document, not the standard it formalizes. Every released version stays resolvable at its version IRI, and the content there never changes. Earlier publications carried no version IRI, and their owl:versionInfo restated the version of the standard."@en ;
